      "content": "When dealing with undisclosed or offshore assets in an international estate, both the UK Inheritance Tax (IHT) and US estate tax laws become relevant. Generally, tax authorities require full disclosure of all worldwide assets belonging to the deceased individual. Failing to disclose assets can lead to severe penalties, investigations, and potentially substantial tax liabilities in both jurisdictions. Professional legal and tax advice specialized in cross-border estates is absolutely crucial to navigate these complex compliance issues correctly.",
